&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Joining Collibra’s Accounts Payable team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an AP Analyst, you will oversee our global financial obligations, ensuring high-precision execution across a complex multi-entity ecosystem.&amp;nbsp;In this role, you will lead full-cycle operations while building key partnerships with Procurement, Treasury, and Total Rewards to drive organizational success.You will be a vital contributor to our AI-driven initiatives, helping us mature our processes and optimize departmental performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Senior AP Manager, you will impact our culture by being respectfully direct and ensuring our financial workflows show up to win.&amp;nbsp;This is a selling opportunity to grow your career within a fast-paced and innovative finance environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid role based in our Raleigh office. Our hybrid model means you’ll work from the office at least two days each week. This setup helps us stay connected, work more closely together, and keep making progress as a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accounts Payable Analysts at Collibra are responsible for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executing full-cycle AP operations&lt;/strong&gt; with high precision across a complex global ecosystem of multiple entities and currencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partnering with Procurement and Treasury&lt;/strong&gt; to manage financial obligations while supporting AI-driven initiatives to enhance departmental efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Processing diverse international invoices&lt;/strong&gt; by applying correct tax treatments (VAT/GST) and ensuring accurate GL coding and PO matching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Driving process automation&lt;/strong&gt; by resolving AI-flagged exceptions, monitoring error queues, and participating in user acceptance testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Managing global pay cycles&lt;/strong&gt; to ensure timely vendor payments and precise month-end reconciliations in alignment with internal controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s degree in finance or accounting, or at least 5 years of experience in a high-volume AP role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience with NetSuite or comparable ERP systems, alongside tools like Zip, Navan, or Brex.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intermediate proficiency in Excel, specifically utilizing VLOOKUPs and pivot tables for data analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with international banking requirements and various regional payment methods (ACH, SEPA, BACS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work within automated or AI-assisted financial workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possessing a proactive working style with a deep commitment to accuracy and meeting tight deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative team player who thrives in fast-paced environments and takes full ownership of independent tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer-service focused, maintaining a positive attitude and strong interpersonal skills when resolving complex issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An adaptable learner interested in how emerging technologies and AI can optimize traditional accounting functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strategic thinker who identifies systemic issues and proposes effective solutions for process improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measures of success&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within your first month, you will master the end-to-end P2P cycle and integrate with our core tools and AI initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within your third month, you will lead the accurate processing of AP invoices and participate in automated testing cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within your sixth month, you will achieve complete ownership of global AP functions and independently resolve AI exceptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation for this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The standard base salary range for this position is $52,000 - $65,000 per year. This position is not eligible for additional commission-based compensation. Salary offers are based on a combination of factors, including, but not limited to, experience, skills, and location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to base salary, we offer a competitive total rewards package, including bonus potential, equity for eligible roles, a Flex Fund monthly stipend, pension/401k plans, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Benefits at Collibra&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collibra recognizes and values that everyone has different needs, interests, and life goals. We built our benefits program with flexibility in mind to support you and your loved ones through a diverse range of circumstances and life events. These flexible offerings sit on a foundation of competitive compensation, health coverage, and time off. Learn more about &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.collibra.com/us/en/company/careers/benefits&quot;&gt;Collibra’s benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We create inclusion and belonging through how we onboard, meet, connect, engage, and communicate. Learn more about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.collibra.com/us/en/company/careers/dei&quot;&gt;diversity, equity, and inclusion&lt;/a&gt; at Collibra.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Collibra, we’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We realize the key to creating a company with a world-class culture and employee experience comes from who we hire and creating a workplace that celebrates everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With this, we proudly consider qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, pregnancy, sex, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, physical or mental disability, HIV status, registered domestic partner status, caregiver status, marital status, veteran or military status, citizenship status or any other legally protected category. If you have a need that requires accommodation, let us know by completing our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.collibra.com/us/en/company/careers/accommodations&quot;&gt;Accommodations for Applicants form&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Joining Collibra&#39;s Talent Management &amp;amp; Development team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is fundamentally reshaping how organizations operate. At Collibra, we believe realizing the value of AI requires more than great technology, it depends on how confidently people adopt it and apply it in their everyday work. Building the skills, confidence and mindset to work alongside AI will be critical to how we innovate, collaborate and create value for customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an AI Enablement Manager who is passionate about helping employees confidently adopt AI and identify practical opportunities to rethink the way work gets done. You&#39;ll combine strong hands-on AI experience with coaching, enablement and learning to help employees integrate AI into their workflows and accelerate AI adoption across the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Director of Talent Management &amp;amp; Development, you&#39;ll lead our AI enablement initiatives, partner closely with Product &amp;amp; Engineering, and help teams identify opportunities to use AI, rethink the way work gets done, and adopt new ways of working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid role based in our Brussels office. Our hybrid model means you’ll work from the office at least two days each week. This setup helps us stay connected, work more closely together, and keep making progress as a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Enablement Managers at Collibra are responsible for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accelerate AI Adoption&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and design Collibra&#39;s AI enablement approach and programs to build AI maturity and accelerate the adoption of AI tools and new ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with leaders across the business to understand workflows and identify high-value AI and automation opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help teams evaluate opportunities based on business impact, feasibility and responsible AI practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead an impactful AI Mentor network that drives AI adoption and surfaces learning needs and opportunities across functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach leaders, teams and employees to identify AI opportunities, build practical solutions and integrate AI into how work gets done&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning Experience Design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deliver engaging workshops, enablement experiences, self-paced learning and practical guidance tailored to different audiences and skill levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create scalable resources and tools that help employees discover, reuse and build on AI use cases, best practices and learning across the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure AI maturity and sustainable adoption, and gather business feedback to evaluate and continuously improve our enablement approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously evolve enablement approaches by leveraging AI, emerging technologies and learning best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product &amp;amp; Engineering Learning Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and deliver the Product &amp;amp; Engineering onboarding program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product &amp;amp; Engineering leaders to identify learning and enablement priorities, including opportunities to support AI adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate enterprise learning initiatives into relevant experiences for technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Product &amp;amp; Engineering as ways of working and organizational priorities continue to evolve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building practical AI solutions, including agents and automated workflows, to solve business problems and improve how work gets done&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience assessing business processes and identifying opportunities to improve them through AI and automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional ability to explain technical concepts to non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coaching others to confidently adopt AI and new ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience facilitating engaging workshops and leading enablement sessions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management, stakeholder management and analytical skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about AI and emerging technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Naturally curious and eager to experiment with new tools and ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An engaging facilitator, coach and communicator&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable navigating ambiguity and translating ideas into practical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and skilled at building partnerships across the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized and able to manage multiple initiatives simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measures of success&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Within your first 3 months, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships across the business and establish yourself as a credible AI coach and advisor to key stakeholders, AI Mentors and Product &amp;amp; Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess Collibra&#39;s current AI enablement approach and get sign-off from the People leadership team on a prioritized roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess and relaunch the AI Mentor network with clear expectations, priorities, resources and ways of working focused on driving AI adoption within each function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run your first AI workshops, resulting in clear AI opportunities and next steps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of Product &amp;amp; Engineering onboarding and align with P&amp;amp;E leaders on priority learning and enablement needs, including how you can support their evolving use of AI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Within your first 6 months, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build an active AI Mentor network that, with your coaching and support, drives AI adoption and surfaces learning needs and AI opportunities within each function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach teams and functions to identify high-value AI opportunities, build practical AI solutions and embed AI into how work gets done, with at least 5 shipped or piloted working solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish scalable ways for employees to discover, reuse and build on AI use cases, best practices and resources across Collibra&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear success measures and a consistent approach to demonstrating the impact of Collibra&#39;s AI enablement investments on a quarterly basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver targeted learning and enablement with Product &amp;amp; Engineering that supports evolving ways of working and AI adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Within your first 12 months, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate measurable progress in AI maturity across Collibra, with employees progressing to Perform on the AI Maturity Grid and teams using AI to drive meaningful outcomes (such as time saved, quality improved, number of processes automated)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a trusted AI enablement partner across the business, with functions proactively engaging you to identify where AI can create value and build the skills and solutions to realize it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead an AI Mentor network with measurable output, such as number of use cases surfaced, solutions shipped, workshops run, employees coached per quarter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Benefits at Collibra&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collibra recognizes and values that everyone has different needs, interests, and life goals. We built our benefits program with flexibility in mind to support you and your loved ones through a diverse range of circumstances and life events. These flexible offerings sit on a foundation of competitive compensation, health coverage, and time off. Learn more about &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.collibra.com/us/en/company/careers/benefits&quot;&gt;Collibra’s benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We create inclusion and belonging through how we onboard, meet, connect, engage, and communicate. Learn more about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.collibra.com/us/en/company/careers/dei&quot;&gt;diversity, equity, and inclusion&lt;/a&gt; at Collibra.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Collibra, we’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We realize the key to creating a company with a world-class culture and employee experience comes from who we hire and creating a workplace that celebrates everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With this, we proudly consider qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, pregnancy, sex, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, physical or mental disability, HIV status, registered domestic partner status, caregiver status, marital status, veteran or military status, citizenship status or any other legally protected category. If you have a need that requires accommodation, let us know by completing our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.collibra.com/us/en/company/careers/accommodations&quot;&gt;Accommodations for Applicants form&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Joining Collibra’s Legal team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collibra is seeking a Commercial Counsel to join our high-impact Legal team. You will be a key individual responsible for drafting, negotiating, and closing enterprise SaaS, software, and technology-related agreements that power Collibra&#39;s growth. This role provides critical legal and commercial support to our Sales and Procurement organizations, ensuring Collibra continues to close deals quickly while staying protected on risk, compliance, and contractual terms. You will act as a trusted legal partner to the business, working closely with Sales, Finance, Security, and Procurement to move deals forward without cutting corners on legal protection.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid role based in our Brussels office. Our hybrid model means you’ll work from the office at least two days each week. This setup helps us stay connected, work more closely together, and keep making progress as a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial Counsels at Collibra are responsible for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drafting, reviewing, and negotiating enterprise SaaS, software, and technology agreements including partnership, reseller, supply, and licensing agreements to support Collibra&#39;s commercial relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing the commercial contracting process to keep deals moving efficiently while protecting Collibra&#39;s legal interests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering with Sales, Sales Operations, Finance, Security, and Procurement teams to drive transactions to successful completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advising on the structure of customer arrangements to support sound legal and business decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitoring regulatory and legal developments, and advising on related legal matters arising from Collibra&#39;s operations, to help the company stay ahead of compliance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of relevant legal experience, preferably as in-house commercial contracts counsel in the software industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A law degree and qualification to practice in an EU or EEA jurisdiction, the UK, or the US (or equivalent experience). Belgian bar admission is not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English and French, with the ability to draft and negotiate in both languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated proficiency in leveraging AI tools (e.g., Claude, Gemini, ChatGPT, Harvey) to solve real-world business challenges, drive measurable outcomes, and&amp;nbsp; streamline workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of GDPR and data protection concepts as they apply to SaaS contracting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience negotiating with large enterprise or public sector customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Someone who applies strong drafting and negotiation skills, grounded in excellent business judgment and critical thinking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Someone who attends to detail, catching nuances in complex commercial agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Someone who communicates with a service-oriented approach, building trusted relationships with legal and non-legal colleagues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Someone who prioritizes and manages multiple tasks and stakeholders simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Someone who takes initiative, identifying and acting on opportunities without waiting for direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measures of success&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within your first month, you will get familiar with Collibra&#39;s product, contracting processes, and risk appetite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within your third month, you will independently negotiate contracts with enterprise customers and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within your sixth month, you will contribute to process improvements and support broader legal projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Benefits at Collibra&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collibra recognizes and values that everyone has different needs, interests, and life goals. We built our benefits program with flexibility in mind to support you and your loved ones through a diverse range of circumstances and life events. These flexible offerings sit on a foundation of competitive compensation, health coverage, and time off. Learn more about &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.collibra.com/us/en/company/careers/benefits&quot;&gt;Collibra’s benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We create inclusion and belonging through how we onboard, meet, connect, engage, and communicate. Learn more about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.collibra.com/us/en/company/careers/dei&quot;&gt;diversity, equity, and inclusion&lt;/a&gt; at Collibra.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Collibra, we’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We realize the key to creating a company with a world-class culture and employee experience comes from who we hire and creating a workplace that celebrates everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With this, we proudly consider qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, pregnancy, sex, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, physical or mental disability, HIV status, registered domestic partner status, caregiver status, marital status, veteran or military status, citizenship status or any other legally protected category. If you have a need that requires accommodation, let us know by completing our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.collibra.com/us/en/company/careers/accommodations&quot;&gt;Accommodations for Applicants form&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Joining Collibra&#39;s Software Engineering team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you interested in ushering a new era of data participation? Collibra is shaping the way companies manage data by helping customers connect the right data, insights, and algorithms for all Data Citizens. When everyone across the organization is enabled with data, true transformation can take place. We are building a team of exceptional people to help us deliver on that promise. If you are interested in a career at the leading edge of technology, we look forward to hearing from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a DevOps Software Engineer to join us on the development of our Edge Platform. This team is responsible for providing a framework that allows Engineers to easily integrate, deploy, upgrade, and manage Edge applications within the Collibra platform ecosystem for our customers. You&#39;ll focus on the infrastructure, tooling, and automation that make this platform reliable and easy to operate at scale. We are an engineering-driven company where your talent and skills are truly appreciated and maximized.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid role based in our Prague office. Our hybrid model means you&#39;ll work from the office at least two days each week. This setup helps us stay connected, work more closely together, and keep making progress as a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DevOps Software Engineers at Collibra are responsible for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing, building, and maintaining customer-facing deployment, upgrade, and lifecycle management workflows for the Edge Platform across a wide range of Kubernetes environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operating and improving Kubernetes-based environments across on-premises and cloud infrastructure, spanning a variety of distributions and customer configurations, with a focus on reliability, scalability, and observability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing and maintaining platform tooling that enables customers and internal teams to deploy, monitor, and troubleshoot Edge applications efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with Product Managers, Architects, and other engineering teams to ensure infrastructure and operational needs are integrated into the product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participating in incident response, post-incident reviews, and driving improvements to system reliability and operational processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in a DevOps, SRE, or infrastructure-focused software engineering role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry experience and knowledge of:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Docker, Kubernetes (including familiarity with diverse distributions such as EKS, AKS, GKE, OpenShift, or k3s), and Helm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud infrastructure fundamentals across one or more major providers (AWS, GCP, Azure).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CI/CD systems (e.g., Jenkins, GitHub Actions, GitLab CI).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Java and/or Go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with infrastructure-as-code concepts and tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A solid understanding of cloud-native and on-premises application deployment, networking, and observability (logging, metrics, tracing).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience using AI tools to drive outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent related working experience is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You must have work authorization to work in Prague, CZ.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited to do your best work with a diverse and distributed team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about automation, reliability, and reducing operational toil.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable building and operating systems on Kubernetes across diverse environments, from managed cloud services to on-premises clusters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive and clear communicator, skilled at articulating technical concepts to both engineering and business partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An advocate for continuous learning and improvement for yourself and the technology you build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measures of success&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Within your first month&lt;/strong&gt;, you will familiarize yourself with the Edge product, infrastructure, deployment pipelines, and team, and be contributing your first changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Within your third month&lt;/strong&gt;, you will be comfortable owning and improving deployment workflows, infrastructure configuration, and operational processes independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Within your sixth month&lt;/strong&gt;, you will be driving significant infrastructure or platform tooling initiatives and contributing to the team&#39;s reliability and operational strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Benefits at Collibra&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collibra recognizes and values that everyone has different needs, interests, and life goals. We built our benefits program with flexibility in mind to support you and your loved ones through a diverse range of circumstances and life events. These flexible offerings sit on a foundation of competitive compensation, health coverage, and time off. Learn more about &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.collibra.com/us/en/company/careers/benefits&quot;&gt;Collibra’s benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
