&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Joining Collibra&#39;s Growth Marketing Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collibra&#39;s Growth Marketing team is moving to an AI-first operating model built around four functions and we&#39;re looking for a Director of Field, ABM &amp;amp; Events to own the regional pipeline number for NAM and EMEA. Reporting to the VP of Growth Marketing, you&#39;ll lead a team of senior field marketers who are full ABM owners for their territories, and manage Global Events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll partner closely with Integrated Marketing, Partner Marketing, and Marketing Ops to keep field strategy aligned to pipeline goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Values-in-action (We show up to win): This team is being asked to change how it works and what it&#39;s measured on this role exists to make that transformation land, and to keep the team moving with urgency toward the pipeline number.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is remote.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Directors of Field ABM &amp;amp; Events at Collibra are responsible for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the NAM and EMEA pipeline P&amp;amp;L accountable to a pipeline number, not an activity plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading the ABM operating rhythm across all four field marketers: weekly account intelligence briefing consumption, AVP alignment, activation, and loop closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the NAM and EMEA territory coverage models, defining the handshake between vertical/strategic and regional field marketers and holding both accountable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing the Global Events Manager, owning the handshake between event production and field-led account strategy events runs the room, field owns the accounts in it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Representing field marketing in quarterly ICP alignment sessions with the CRO and AVPs, and owning account tier nominations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in B2B enterprise field marketing with direct pipeline accountability, not solely event execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a team of five or more direct reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering directly with AVP-level sales leaders, including forecast calls and QBRs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated proficiency in leveraging AI tools (e.g., Claude, Gemini, ChatGPT, Copilot) to solve real-world business challenges, drive measurable outcomes, or streamline workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent related working experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in ABM program design 6sense or equivalent, account tier frameworks, and 1:Few programs build alongside a field motion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced managing a team through significant change, bringing change-management skill to a field-to-ABM transformation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sensitive to regional differences across NAM and EMEA, whether through lived or managed experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable holding a team accountable through transition two open hires landing mid-year, a direct report being repositioned, and a new operating rhythm being embedded.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-native, designing AI-augmented workflows for pipeline forecasting, account research, and briefing automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measures of Success&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within your first month, you will: complete onboarding, meet the team, and the two incoming field hires, and audit the current NAM/EMEA territory coverage and pipeline baseline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within your third month, you will: run your first AVP alignment calls across NAM and EMEA, formalize the weekly account intelligence briefing rhythm, and establish the events-field handshake with Sarah.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within your sixth month, you will: show measurable pipeline contribution from the ABM motion across all four territories, and demonstrate the team operating as account-led pipeline owners rather than event operators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation for this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The standard base salary range for this position is $168,000.00 - $210,000.00 per year. This position is not eligible for additional commission-based compensation. Salary offers are based on a combination of factors, including, but not limited to, experience, skills, and location.&lt;/p&gt;
