&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Joining Collibra’s Workplace Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Collibra, we believe that a great workplace is more than just a space, it’s a place where people feel connected, supported, and set up for success. To ensure continued success in our evolution, we’re looking for a hands-on, hospitality driven Senior Workplace Specialist who will lead the day-to-day operations of our Raleigh office while also providing operational support for Collibra’s global employee experience and onboarding programs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll be the go-to person for all things workplace in Raleigh, acting as a trusted resource for employees and visitors alike. You’ll play a key role in shaping the local culture, supporting company-wide programs, and delivering a seamless, welcoming workplace experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a great opportunity for someone who enjoys building, thrives in a fast-paced environment, and brings both operational rigor and a strong service mindset. You’ll be part of our global People and Places team, reporting directly to the Senior Manager, Workplace and Real Estate with a dotted-line partnership to Employee Experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid role based in our Raleigh office. This role is expected to work from our Raleigh office 4 days per week. This setup helps us stay connected, work more closely together, and keep making progress as a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Workplace and Experience Specialists at Collibra are responsible for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Workplace responsibilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead day-to-day workplace operations and oversee the experience in our Raleigh office.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own key workplace programs in Raleigh such as food, supplies, mail, office supplies, and visitor support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the main point of contact for Raleigh workplace needs, welcoming guests, assisting employees, and coordinating with building management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to and manage workplace service tickets globally, escalating issues when necessary and ensuring timely resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support event logistics, such as team offsites, customer visits, leadership sessions, and employee engagement activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the new hire onboarding experience locally, fostering meaningful local connections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and execute events like anniversaries, social gatherings, and lunch &amp;amp; learns in Raleigh.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track vendor spend and help manage local budgets; work with Procurement to onboard and manage vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the global Workplace team’s lead for data and tooling, supporting the team’s efforts to make informed decisions and improve performance, as well as drive Workplace’s AI initiatives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with local health, safety, and environmental standards in Raleigh.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to sustainability and inclusion initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain close relationships with Raleigh employees and use their feedback to shape local workplace programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the implementation of global workplace programs, adapting them to fit the Raleigh context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employee Experience responsibilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide operational and administrative support for new hire orientation and onboarding programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate the scheduling, logistics, and communications for virtual orientation and onboarding sessions, including Zoom facilitation support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the execution of quarterly live onboarding events, including logistics, onsite coordination, materials, and attendee experience data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage onboarding-related operational tasks such as calendar coordination, facilitator support, room setup, materials preparation, and post-session logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute ideas and feedback from a workplace perspective to help continuously improve the onboarding and employee experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support cross-functional coordination with People Ops, IT, Workplace, and SMEs to ensure new hires are set up for success from day one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–4 years of experience in workplace or employee experience roles; experience as an office site lead preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work 4 days per week&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;onsite in Raleigh&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting hybrid work environments and delivering solutions that support a distributed workforce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with vendor management, budgeting, onboarding support, event logistics, and employee engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across time zones or in global teams, with an understanding of how to adapt support accordingly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physically able to stand, move, lift, and carry items as needed (up to 50lbs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated proficiency in leveraging AI tools (e.g., Claude, Gemini, ChatGPT, Copilot) to solve real-world business challenges, drive measurable outcomes, or streamline workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s degree or equivalent related working experience is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hospitality-driven and passionate about creating welcoming, well-run office environments and positive employee experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive and resourceful, with a knack for solving problems and anticipating needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear communicator, comfortable with verbal and written communication, signage, and internal messaging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented and organized, with a strong ability to manage competing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A team player who collaborates well across departments such as IT, Finance, and People.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open to feedback and constantly seeking ways to improve the employee experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with a dual-reporting structure and independently managing day-to-day tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to jump in and tackle any task, regardless of how large or small.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measures of success&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within your first month, you’ve built relationships with the team and developed a strong understanding of the Raleigh office and core workplace operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within your third month, you’ve established trust with key stakeholders, internal teams, and vendors and are routinely supporting any immediate workplace or onboarding operational needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within your sixth month, you’re driving noticeable improvements in workplace and employee experience, aligned with Collibra’s growth and employee engagement goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation for this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The standard base salary range for this position is $60,000.00 - $75,000.00 per year.&amp;nbsp; This position is not eligible for additional commission-based compensation. Salary offers are based on a combination of factors, including, but not limited to, experience, skills, and location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to base salary, we offer a competitive total rewards package, including bonus potential, equity for eligible roles, a Flex Fund monthly stipend, pension/401k plans, and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Benefits at Collibra&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collibra recognizes and values that everyone has different needs, interests, and life goals. We built our benefits program with flexibility in mind to support you and your loved ones through a diverse range of circumstances and life events. These flexible offerings sit on a foundation of competitive compensation, health coverage, and time off. Learn more about &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.collibra.com/us/en/company/careers/benefits&quot;&gt;Collibra’s benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We create inclusion and belonging through how we onboard, meet, connect, engage, and communicate. Learn more about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.collibra.com/us/en/company/careers/dei&quot;&gt;diversity, equity, and inclusion&lt;/a&gt; at Collibra.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Collibra, we’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We realize the key to creating a company with a world-class culture and employee experience comes from who we hire and creating a workplace that celebrates everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With this, we proudly consider qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, pregnancy, sex, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, physical or mental disability, HIV status, registered domestic partner status, caregiver status, marital status, veteran or military status, citizenship status or any other legally protected category. If you have a need that requires accommodation, let us know by completing our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.collibra.com/us/en/company/careers/accommodations&quot;&gt;Accommodations for Applicants form&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Joining Collibra’s Support team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re shaping the way some of the largest organizations in the world manage data by helping customers connect the right data and insights for all Data Citizens. We are building a team of exceptional people to help us deliver on that promise. As a Technical Account Engineer, you are Collibra&#39;s highest-touch technical presence within a named customer account. You serve as the customer&#39;s dedicated technical expert owning the support experience end-to-end, driving proactive risk management, and acting as the trusted technical advisor bridging Collibra&#39;s product and engineering teams with the customer&#39;s own technical stakeholders. You build trust through technical credibility, not account management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid role based in our Raleigh, NC or New York, NY office. Our hybrid model means you’ll work from the office at least two days each week. This setup helps us stay connected, work more closely together, and keep making progress as a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Account Engineers at Collibra are responsible for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serving as the primary technical contact for a named portfolio of Premium accounts, with full SLA accountability and end-to-end ticket ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acting as the first escalation point for complex or sensitive issues, engaging Engineering and specialist teams where required and prioritizing based on business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identifying risks through ticket trend analysis, environment health monitoring, and release gap assessments — flagging structural concerns before they become incidents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advising customers on upgrade paths, release readiness, and optimal timing to ensure environment stability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivering Knowledge Share Sessions tailored to each customer&#39;s environment and active use cases, with a minimum of two sessions per account per year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conducting bi-annual Support Reviews and preparing quarterly account briefings for Account Executives ahead of QBRs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guiding customers on Mutual Success Plan milestones, adoption blockers, and best practices to drive long-term value realization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surfacing expansion signals, upsell opportunities, and churn risk indicators to the Account Executive and Customer Engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with Engineering and Product on trends, bugs, and feature prioritization for named accounts, and contributing to internal knowledge base and playbook improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in a technical support, technical account management, customer engineering, or solutions engineering role within an enterprise SaaS environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on technical skills including Java, REST API, SSO, LDAP, Kubernetes, VM environments, SQL, and SSL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with root cause analysis, systematic debugging, and integration architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad knowledge of data governance, data catalog, data quality, or data management platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of managing complex technical relationships with enterprise customers across multiple stakeholders and teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated proficiency in leveraging AI tools (e.g., Claude, Gemini, ChatGPT, Copilot) to solve real-world business challenges, drive measurable outcomes, or streamline workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s degree or equivalent related working experience is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A trusted technical advisor who builds credibility through depth of knowledge and problem resolution not relationship management alone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An effective communicator, comfortable engaging architects, data engineers, platform administrators, and executive stakeholders alike.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive by nature, you identify and surface risks before they escalate, and take ownership of systemic issues through to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative partner who works across Engineering, Product, and GTM teams to drive outcomes for your customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resilient and composed under pressure, with the ability to manage escalations and competing priorities across a portfolio of accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited about continuous learning and development within the data governance space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to travel as needed for strategic or at-risk account visits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measures of success&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within your first month, you will become familiar with Collibra&#39;s product suite, Premium Support model, and your assigned account portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within your second month, you will have established cadence with your accounts, taken ownership of active tickets, and delivered your first account health assessments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within your third month, you will be operating as a trusted technical advisor across your portfolio — proactively identifying risks, delivering Knowledge Share Sessions, and contributing QBR briefings to your Account Executive counterparts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation for this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The standard base salary range for this position is $116,000 – $145,000 per year. Salary offers are based on a combination of factors, including, but not limited to, experience, skills, and location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to base salary, we offer a competitive total rewards package, including bonus potential, equity for eligible roles, a Flex Fund monthly stipend, pension/401k plans, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
